# ── PyInstaller build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
workspace/_build/
workspace/**/__pycache__/
workspace/**/*.pyc
workspace/**/*.pyo

# ── Secrets — never commit real tokens/credentials ────────────────────────────
# The real config (contains Discord token). The safe copy is nova_gateway - Copy.json
workspace/nova_gateway.json
workspace/openclaw.json
workspace/models/
**/nova_drive_token.json
**/client_secrets.json
**/.env

# ── Runtime / ephemeral files ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
workspace/logs/
workspace/sessions/
workspace/tools/nova_sync/.drive_sync_cache.json
workspace/tools/backups/
workspace/agents/main/sessions/

# ── OS / editor noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo

# ── VM exports & backup artifacts (2026-09-07) ────────────────────────────────
# NovaDrop is the shared drop folder between Nova's computer and the host, and it is
# where SNAPSHOT.cmd writes `wsl --export` images. A 1.07 GB tar landed in three
# auto-commits on 2026-09-06 and GitHub rejects anything over 100 MB, so every watcher
# push failed from then on. Source checkpoints and VM backups need separate homes:
# git holds the code, the tar belongs on a disk/off-machine backup.
NovaDrop/
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.vhdx
*.vhd

# ── Google Drive for Desktop (2026-10-02) ─────────────────────────────────
# Drive backs up this folder and stages its uploads and downloads in these two folders. They
# are Drive's own temp copies, never source. 75,450 of them were auto-committed on 2026-10-01,
# and autosave then committed nothing for 35 hours. See Orient/OPERATIONS.md#lessons-from-incidents
.tmp.driveupload/
.tmp.drivedownload/
# The copy Drive for Desktop syncs instead of this repo (workspace/general_tools/nova_sync/drive_copy.py).
/Nova_Drive/
